      "title": "The Johnson Center for Faculty Development and Excellence in Teaching",
      "description": "Faculty & Staff - Austin College Skip To Main Content Toggle Close Container Close Menu Logo - Mobile Menu Utility Nav Request Info (opens in new window/tab) Apply Visit (opens in new window/tab) Give Campus Offices & Services News & Events Menu Layout Wrapper Menu Logo - Desktop LINKS FOR: New Students Current Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Community Cursive Text Expect the unexpected. Mobile  Kangoroo Image Search Search Clear Search Main Nav Academics Admission & Aid Campus Life Athletics (opens in new window/tab) Mobile Main Nav Academics Majors, Minors & Programs Student Success First-Year Experience Internships JanTerm Admission & Aid Visit (opens in new window/tab) Apply Scholarships Financial Aid Find Your Counselor Campus Life Wellness & Safety Living on Campus Dining Clubs & Greek Life Religious Life Athletics (opens in new window/tab) EXPLORE AUSTIN COLLEGE in words in NUMBERS in PICTURES in OUTCOMES ON A TOUR Menu Image Watermark Header Holder Header Logo Header Right Column Toggle Menu Container Menu Show Container Hovered Hovered Container Toggle Canvas Menu - Container Toggle Menu Canvas Utility Nav - Header Request Info (opens in new window/tab) Apply Visit (opens in new window/tab) Give Campus Offices & Services News & Events In this Section... Horizontal Nav Breadcrumb Faculty & Staff Faculty & Staff Single Hero Students aren’t the only ones who choose Austin College; ’RooNation is also made up of roughly 320 employees - both faculty and staff - who are dedicated to upholding our values and delivering on our mission to educate students in the liberal arts and sciences. An Austin College education emphasizes academic excellence, intellectual and personal integrity, and participation in community life, and it is our dedicated faculty and staff who deliver on that promise. sheild divider Resources for Faculty & Staff Employees who are authenticated through AC's single sign-on can access additional information and resources in the Employee Portal. Employee Portal AC Email Moodle Self-Service Password Reset Directory (Faculty & Staff) Academic Calendar Austin College Bulletin Title IX Lake Campus Proud to be a part of #RooNation? Bring a little campus spirit to your screen or celebration. Explore the Media Kit for printable decorations and digital wallpapers. AC Decor & Wallpapers Join the Austin College Community Be part of a community that values you and your talents and is committed to your long term success as a professional. OPEN EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITIES Human Resources Office Employee Programs The Johnson Center for Faculty Development and Excellence in Teaching Center for Staff Development Staff Council Employee Wellness | Live Well at Austin College The Johnson Center for Faculty Development and Excellence in Teaching Or, the “Johnson Center” as it is affectionately known, offers programs throughout the year to our faculty to help them develop as teachers, as academics, and as people. Professional development for faculty starts with new faculty orientation and continues through all stages of a faculty member’s career. Learn More Center for Staff Development The Austin College Center for Staff Development offers programs each year to help our professional community develop as managers, supervisors, administrative professionals, individual contributors, and as people. The programs and resources offered by the Center for Staff Development are designed to encourage skills assessment, workplace accountability, and a culture of well-being to help us be our best as individuals as we deliver on the mission of Austin College. Staff Council Staff Council is made up of employees representing every division of the college. They organize community events throughout the year for staff and faculty fellowship, and also assure that the staff of the institution have a voice in addressing concerns related to campus employment. Employee Wellness | Live Well at Austin College Austin College and our health insurance consortium, CARES, are committed to creating a culture of wellbeing for Austin College employees and their spouses and dependents. Utilizing the book “Well Being: The Five Essential Elements” by Tom Rath and Jim Harter, the Live Well team offers support for five different aspects of wellbeing: physical, financial, social, community, and purpose – from yoga classes for employees and spouses to retirement counseling! Discover 'RooNation & the Surrounding Area Why Work at Austin College Austin College is committed to excellence in residential, undergraduate education in the liberal arts and sciences. Faculty and staff describe the college’s students as intellectually curious, adventurous, open-minded, and engaged in their communities. Read More about Why Work at Austin College Points of Distinction Austin College, founded in 1849, is Texas' oldest higher education institution still operating under its original name and charter. While rooted in a covenant with the Presbyterian Church (USA), it fosters an inclusive atmosphere supporting all religious traditions. Read More about Points of Distinction Sherman & Surrounding Area Austin College is located in Sherman, Texas , at the heart of the burgeoning north Texas technology corridor. Sherman and Denison, our nearest neighbor, are home to many beautiful outdoor recreation areas, parks, and more. Read More about Sherman & Surrounding Area < > Explore Austin College in words Hear what our community has to say about Austin College. IN WORDS in NUMBERS Sometimes you just want the facts; this is the page for you. IN NUMBERS in PICTURES Explore a day in the life of a student. IN PICTURES in OUTCOMES Catch a glimpse of your future as you meet our Alumni who are making their way in this global world. IN OUTCOMES ON A TOUR Get to know our spaces and places around campus. ON A TOUR Footer Holder Footer Logo Footer Address 900 N. Grand Avenue Sherman TX 75090 903-813-2000 Socials Facebook (opens in new window/tab) YouTube (opens in new window/tab) Instagram (opens in new window/tab) LinkedIn (opens in new window/tab) Quick Links Campus Conduct Hotline Mental Health Resources Human Resources Title IX Office Consumer Information Connect Request Info (opens in new window/tab) Subscribe (opens in new window/tab) Contact Us Directory Login Student Portal (opens in new window/tab) Employee Portal (opens in new window/tab) Outlook Email (opens in new window/tab) Self-Service (opens in new window/tab) Footer Statement Austin College is committed to equal opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, national origin, race, religion, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, citizenship status, genetic information, status as a veteran, or any other characteristic that is protected by applicable state or federal law in its operations, employment opportunities, educational programs, and related activities. This commitment is supported by policies applied in a manner consistent with governing state and federal regulations. The following people have been designated to handle complaints: For all Students, Employees, and Others: Melanie Oelfke Powered by Finalsite"
