    "https://www.austincollege.edu/details/~board/jobs/post/assistant-professor-of-kinesiology": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Kinesiology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Kinesiology | Details Skip To Main Content Toggle Close Container Close Menu Logo - Mobile Menu Utility Nav Request Info (opens in new window/tab) Apply Visit (opens in new window/tab) Give Campus Offices & Services News & Events Menu Layout Wrapper Menu Logo - Desktop LINKS FOR: New Students Current Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Community Cursive Text Expect the unexpected. Mobile  Kangoroo Image Search Search Clear Search Main Nav Academics Admission & Aid Campus Life Athletics (opens in new window/tab) Mobile Main Nav Academics Majors, Minors & Programs Student Success First-Year Experience Internships JanTerm Admission & Aid Visit (opens in new window/tab) Apply Scholarships Financial Aid Find Your Counselor Campus Life Wellness & Safety Living on Campus Dining Clubs & Greek Life Religious Life Athletics (opens in new window/tab) EXPLORE AUSTIN COLLEGE in words in NUMBERS in PICTURES in OUTCOMES ON A TOUR Menu Image Watermark Header Holder Header Logo Header Right Column Toggle Menu Container Menu Show Container Hovered Hovered Container Toggle Canvas Menu - Container Toggle Menu Canvas Utility Nav - Header Request Info (opens in new window/tab) Apply Visit (opens in new window/tab) Give Campus Offices & Services News & Events In this Section... Horizontal Nav Breadcrumb Assistant Professor of Kinesiology The Austin College Department of Kinesiology invites applications for a Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Kinesiology beginning in August of 2027. The Kinesiology Department is seeking an energetic and collaborative Assistant Professor who holds a doctorate degree (Ph.D., Ed.D. or equivalent) in kinesiology, public health, rehabilitation science, health sciences, or a related and complementary field. We seek a colleague who can contribute to teaching introductory, intermediate, and advanced courses within the Kinesiology program, to include foundational courses as well as specialty courses aligned with the candidate’s expertise. We are especially interested in candidates whose specialty courses can also support the Public Health program at Austin College. The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to undergraduate teaching in a liberal arts environment and an interest in mentoring students with diverse academic and career goals, including those pursuing graduate study and health-related professions. Austin College is a leading national private liberal arts college located north of Dallas in Sherman, Texas. Founded in 1849, it is the oldest institution of higher education in Texas operating under original charter and name. Recognized nationally for academic excellence in the areas of international education, pre-professional training, and leadership studies, the College provides an academically challenging and lively community of students, staff, and faculty committed to intellectual growth through individual and collaborative endeavors. Austin College (AC) is one of 40 schools profiled in Loren Pope’s influential book, Colleges That Change Lives . Candidates should send the following: letter of application CV copies of graduate transcripts (unofficial are sufficient for the application) statement of teaching philosophy, no more than one page statement of research, no more than one page a statement reflecting on the composition of our student body and outlining how they would engage all our students in their teaching, scholarship, and/or service. Please combine materials into one PDF document and email it to our Kinesiology Search team . Three references should send recommendation letters directly to the aforementioned email address with the candidate’s name in the subject line. For full consideration, applications must be received by October 9, 2026 . Initial video conference interviews will occur in mid-October 2026 and on-campus interviews in late October through mid-November 2026. Austin College is an Equal Opportunity Employer that serves a diverse student body and is committed to the same in the hiring process. Applicants must be authorized to work for Austin College at the time employment begins. Faculty Positions Footer Holder Footer Logo Footer Address 900 N. Grand Avenue Sherman TX 75090 903-813-2000 Socials Facebook (opens in new window/tab) YouTube (opens in new window/tab) Instagram (opens in new window/tab) LinkedIn (opens in new window/tab) Quick Links Campus Conduct Hotline Mental Health Resources Human Resources Title IX Office Consumer Information Connect Request Info (opens in new window/tab) Subscribe (opens in new window/tab) Contact Us Directory Login Student Portal (opens in new window/tab) Employee Portal (opens in new window/tab) Outlook Email (opens in new window/tab) Self-Service (opens in new window/tab) Footer Statement Austin College is committed to equal opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, national origin, race, religion, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, citizenship status, genetic information, status as a veteran, or any other characteristic that is protected by applicable state or federal law in its operations, employment opportunities, educational programs, and related activities. This commitment is supported by policies applied in a manner consistent with governing state and federal regulations. The following people have been designated to handle complaints: For all Students, Employees, and Others: Melanie Oelfke Powered by Finalsite"
